          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Various structures in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            have a classification into 10 classes, more or less explicitly related to the 2 + 8
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            up to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+periodicity"} Bott periodicity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            and 8 for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR"} KR
          %p
            The specific term “10-fold way” is a variation of the term “threefold way” used in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Dyson62"} Dyson 1962
            %a{:href => "#HHZ04"} Heinzner, Huckleberry &amp; Zirnbauer 2004
            and
            %a{:href => "#Z10"} Zirnbauer 2010
            in reference to work going back to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AZ97"} Altland &amp; Zirnbauer 1997
            %a{:href => "#Z10"} Zirnbauer 2010
            finally speaks at least of the “10-way”).
          %p
            The term became rather popular in the wake of the seminal suggestion by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kitaev09"} Kitaev 2009
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SchnyderRyuFurusakiLudwig2008"} Schnyder, Ryu, Furusaki &amp; Ludwig 2008 table 1
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystalline+topological+insulator"} crystalline
            = succeed "-phases," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
            for more on this.
          %p
            (Though
            %a{:href => "#Kitaev09"} Kitaev 2009
            does not use the term “10-fold way”, either, nor the now standard labels for the ten classes — all this appears later, cf.
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#ChiuTeoSchnyderRyu2016"} Chiu, Teo, Schnyder &amp; Ryu 2016 table 1
          %p
            Kitaev’s suggestion was made more precise by
            %a{:href => "#FreedMoore13"} Freed &amp; Moore 2013
            (who, however and ironically, doubted, on
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1208.5055.pdf#page=57"} p. 57
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2206.13563.pdf#page=2"} pp. 2
            of
            %a{:href => "K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter#SatiSchreiber23"} SS23
            for resolution) and it is these authors who very much amplify (and may have actually coined) the term “10-fold way”. Moreover, they point out (
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1208.5055.pdf#page=75"}> pp. 75
            ) that a 10-fold classification is already contained by
            = succeed "(!)," do
              %a{:href => "#Dyson62"} Dyson 1962
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+division+algebras"} super division algebras
          %p
            This 10-fold way of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+division+algebras"} super division algebras
            is further amplified in &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Moore13"}> Moore 2013, p. 129
            \&amp;rbrack; and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GeikoMoore2021"} Geiko &amp; Moore 2021
          %p
            The 10-fold way was also approached from a purely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theoretic
            point of view by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RumyninTaylor2021"} Rumynin and Taylor 2021
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+forms"} bilinear forms
            instead of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-linear+maps"} anti-linear maps
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RumyninTaylor2022"} Rumynin and Taylor 2022
          %h2#realizations Realizations
          %div
            %h3#PCTQuantumSymmetries PCT Quantum Symmetries
            %p
              We discuss how
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PCT+symmetry"} PCT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+symmetries"} quantum symmetries
              (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PCTQuantumSymmetry"}
              below) are classified (Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassificationOfPCTQuantumSymmetries"}
              below) by a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10-fold+way"}> 10-fold way
              ” (Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TenFoldWayOfPCTQuantumSymmetries"}
              below).
            %p
              The definition and the argument is quite straightforward. Just for completeness we offer some
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PreliminariesForPCTQuantumSymmetries"} Preliminaries
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PCTQuantumSymmetryDefinitionAndClassification"} Definition and Classification
            %p
              The 10-fold classification of these PCT quantum symmetries immediately induces other incarnations of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10-fold+way"} 10-fold way
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the classification of flavors of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU-theory"}> KU-theory
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
                  in any degree)
                %p
                  (by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-J%C3%A4nich+theorem"} Atiyah-Jänich theorem
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "Atiyah-Jänich+theorem#SummaryInTermsOfGradedFredholmOperators"} in terms of graded Fredholm operators
            %p and with that
            %ul
              %li
                the 10-fold way in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
            %h4#PreliminariesForPCTQuantumSymmetries Preliminaries
            %p Let:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                  be a countably infinite-dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28%E2%84%8B%29"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                  denote its
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antilinear+map"} antilinear
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2^{(t)} \coloneqq \{id, T\}
                  denote the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"} group generated
                  by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              Observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
              with that generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              the group consisting of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
              %em and
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-unitary+operators"} anti-unitary operators
            #eq:GroupOfUnitaryAndAntiUnitaryOperators.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋊
                          %msubsup
                            %mi C
                            %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ∼
                        %mtd
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊔
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mi anti
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi id
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo ,
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi T
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\rtimes
                    C_2^{(t)}
                    \&amp;\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\sqcup
                    \\mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\\
                    (U, id) &amp;\mapsto&amp; U
                    \\\
                    (U, T) &amp;\mapsto&amp; U \circ T
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              This relation passes to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+unitary+groups"} projective unitary groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %msub
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                              %mi anti
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                              %mi anti
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    P \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \&amp;\coloneqq\;
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})/\mathrm{U}(1)
                    \\\
                    P \mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})
                    \&amp;\coloneqq\;
                    \\mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})/\mathrm{U}(1)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              in that we have an analogous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋊
                          %msubsup
                            %mi C
                            %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ∼
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊔
                          %mi P
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mi anti
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mi id
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi U
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    P \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\rtimes
                    C_2^{(t)}
                    \&amp;\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    P\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\sqcup
                    P\mathrm{U}_{anti}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\\
                    ([U], id) &amp;\mapsto&amp; [U]
                    \\\
                    ([U], T) &amp;\mapsto&amp; [U \circ T]
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              This group of
              %em projective unitary/antiunitary operators
              is the group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+symmetries"} quantum symmetries
              as usually considered (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wigner%27s+theorem"}> Wigner's theorem
              ).
            %p
              We next enlarge this a little more to include what may be thought of as particle/antiparticle symmetry, often referred to as
              %em charge conjugation
              symmetry.
            %p To that end, let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mi gr
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo ⊖
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}_{gr} \coloneqq \mathscr{H} \ominus \mathscr{H}
                  denote the
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                  the grading
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                  on
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo +
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo −
                                %mo )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo −
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ψ
                                          %mo +
                                %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{array}{ccc}
                        \\mathscr{H}
                        \&amp;\overset{P}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        \\mathscr{H}
                        \\\
                        \\left(
                        \\begin{matrix}
                        \\psi_+
                        \\\
                        \\psi_-
                        \\end{matrix}
                        \\right)
                        \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                        \\left(
                        \\begin{matrix}
                        \\psi_-
                        \\\
                        \\psi_+
                        \\end{matrix}
                        \\right)
                        \\end{array}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2^{(p)} \coloneqq \{id, P\}
                  denote the group generated by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi P
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2^{(c)} \coloneqq \{id, C \coloneqq P T\}
                  denote the group generated by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \circ T
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mi gr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mi gr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ⋊
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}_{gr}(\mathscr{H}_{gr}) \coloneqq \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})^2 \rtimes C_2^{(p)}
                  denote the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
                  which is isomorphic to the subgroup of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mi gr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H}_{gr})
                  on the operators which are of homogeneous degree (either even or odd),
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mi gr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mi gr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋊
                        %msubsup
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\mathrm{U}_{gr}(\mathscr{H}_{gr}) \coloneqq \frac{\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})^2}{\mathrm{U}(1)} \rtimes C_2^{(p)}
                  denote the corresponding projective group
            %p Finally, combine all this to consider the following:
            %h4#PCTQuantumSymmetryDefinitionAndClassification Definition and Classification
            %p
            .num_defn
              %h6 Definition
              %p
                The group of
                %em graded quantum symmetries
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
              #eq:GradedQuantumSymmetries.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi QS
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋊
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msubsup
                        %mi C
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      QS
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\frac{
                      \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})^2
                      }{
                      \\mathrm{U}(1)
                      }
                      \\rtimes
                      \\big(
                      C_2^{(t)} \times C_2^{(c)}
                      \\big)
                      \\mathrlap{\,,}
              %p
                of the even graded projective unitary group with the operations of degree involution
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                and complex involution
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              This is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi QS
                    %mo ↠
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tfrac{
                    \\mathrm{U}(\mathscr{H})^2
                    }{
                    \\mathrm{U}(1)
                    }
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    QS
                    \\twoheadrightarrow
                    C_2^{(t)} \times C_2^{(c)}
            %p of
            #eq:PCTgroup.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mi id
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_2^{(t)} \times C_2^{(c)}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\big\{
                    id, T, C, P \coloneqq C T
                    \\big\}
                    \\,,
            %p
              which we may call the group of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PCT+symmetries"} PCT symmetries
            %p
            #PCTQuantumSymmetry.num_defn
              %h6 Definition
              %p
                A
                %em PCT quantum symmetry
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift"} lift
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                of PCT symmetries
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PCTgroup"} (3)
                to a quantum symmetry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GradedQuantumSymmetries"} (2)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
